      "work": "paper-xi",
      "category": "terminology-consistency",
      "source": {
        "path": "papers/paper-xi/current/publication/source/traditional/Paper_XI_Traditional_Final.tex",
        "line": 1954,
        "expected": "The tensor product splits into two interaction packets of depth twelve. Their total dimension is \\(2\\cdot12=24\\), equal to the product \\(4\\cdot6\\).",
        "reading_passage": "read/paper-xi/finite-examples.html#L1947"
      },
      "context": "Example 17.2 follows the tensor-packet result, which distinguishes carrier dimension and Frobenius coset-cycle length from a possibly shorter interaction-character orbit.",
      "issue": "The example calls twelve a depth, although its displayed lcm and following dimension calculation use twelve as the carrier dimension. Use the terminology of the preceding result.",
